      'Setup example: 36 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win two consecutive hands (deals). The second consecutive win must contain more tricks than the first win.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Trump Calling**: Eldest hand calls trumps after seeing only their first three cards. 2. **Trick Play**: Eldest leads. Players MUST follow suit if possible. 3. **Identical Card Rule**: If two or more identical cards are played to one trick, the one played FIRST wins (if it is the highest rank). 4. **Signalling**: Partners are permitted to signal suit strength via knocks (strong) or tongue-clicks (weak). 5. **Match Resolution**: If a team wins a hand, they must win the next hand with a higher trick count to end the match. If they lose the second hand, the count resets. If they win with fewer tricks, it is a draw and they must try again.',
      "Scoring example: Scoring is binary (Hand won or Hand lost/drawn). Progressive Consecutive Wins: Win Hand A (Tricks > 18), then Win Hand B (Tricks > Hand A's count)..",
